The Internet Archive is a non-profit digital library founded in 1996 by Brewster Kahle and headquartered in San Francisco, California. It provides free access to digitized cultural and historical materials, including web pages, books, software, audio, videos, and images.

Key Features and Collections

• Wayback Machine: Lets users browse historical snapshots of websites and save current web pages for preservation, holding around one trillion archived web pages.
• Texts & Books: Includes tens of millions of texts, public-domain and borrowable books, periodicals, and academic papers.
• Audio & Concerts: Offers millions of audio files, including live concert recordings, radio news archives, and music collections.
• Video & TV: Features millions of videos and television news broadcasts.
• Software & Images: Hosts hundreds of thousands to millions of software programs and digital images.
